        <p class="answer"><span class="hl">A new customs rule stopped all online sales to Norway from 4 August 2026, so orders there fell to almost nothing.</span><a class="fm" href="#sn-hero" id="fm-hero" aria-label="Footnote 1">1</a><span class="sn" id="sn-hero"><b>1</b>Online sales to Norway stopped on 4 August 2026<span class="q">"Parcels from webshops outside Norway are held at the border from 4 August 2026 until further notice."</span><span class="by">Sales, owned by Jon Abara and Sofia Brandt. Checked 3 Oct 2026.</span><span class="dc"><b>Don't conclude:</b> fewer orders there do not mean fewer customers.</span></span></p>

        <h1 class="h1" id="h-hero">Tell your AI agents why the number moved before they guess.</h1>
        <p class="hero-p">Your warehouse knows orders in Norway dropped in August. It doesn't know a customs rule started holding parcels at the border. Someone on your team does.</p>
        <p class="hero-p">Footnote is where they write that down. Once the owner has checked it, agents read it over MCP before they answer. When nothing is written, Footnote says so, and the agent can say so too instead of making something up.</p>
        <div class="hero-cta">
          <a class="btn btn-ink" href="#run">Install</a>
          <a class="btn btn-line" href={docs('get-started')}>Read the docs</a>
        </div>
        <p class="hero-meta">Open source under Apache-2.0. The first release is v0.1.0, and it runs on one computer with Docker.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

