    <!-- Owners -->
    <section class="sec" id="trust" aria-labelledby="h-trust">
      <div class="doc">
        <h2 class="h2" id="h-trust">Agents only see what an owner has published.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Every item belongs to one area, like Sales or Paid media, and the owners of that area decide what goes out. Drafts, suggestions and comments stay inside. Each promise below has a note saying where it's checked.</p>
        <div class="claims">
          <div class="claim"><h3>Drafts stay drafts</h3><p>The database role that answers agents can't read the versions table at all. That's a permission, not a setting someone can flip by accident.<a class="fm" href="#sn-drafts" aria-label="Note 3">3</a><span class="sn" id="sn-drafts"><b>3</b>The test asks as that role and expects <i>permission denied</i>. <a href={repo('tests/integration/mcp.test.ts')}><code>mcp.test.ts</code></a></span></p></div>
          <div class="claim"><h3>A review before it goes live</h3><p>The review holds the claims up against the source. It also replays the questions agents asked against the draft, so the owner sees what will change before it does.</p></div>
          <div class="claim"><h3>Nothing filled in</h3><p>When nothing is written, the answer says Not found and stops. It doesn't reach for a likely story.<a class="fm" href="#sn-nf" aria-label="Note 4">4</a><span class="sn" id="sn-nf"><b>4</b>Golden questions with nothing written down must come back Not found. <a href={repo('db/seed/golden-set.yml')}><code>golden-set.yml</code></a></span></p></div>
          <div class="claim"><h3>What not to conclude</h3><p>An item can say what not to read into it. The Norway one says fewer orders there doesn't mean fewer customers, and the agent gets that line with the item.<a class="fm" href="#sn-dc" aria-label="Note 5">5</a><span class="sn" id="sn-dc"><b>5</b>Sent with the item as <code>not_to_conclude</code>, with the rule "never conclude what it rules out". <a href={repo('src/domain/resolver.ts')}><code>resolver.ts</code></a></span></p></div>
          <div class="claim"><h3>When a definition changes</h3><p>If a definition an item relies on changes or disappears in Cube or dbt, the item is flagged for its owner, and answers say Outdated until they've looked.</p></div>
          <div class="claim"><h3>Topics, not words</h3><p>When an agent asks something, we keep what it was about and how often. We don't keep the words. Your own chats in Ask stay in your browser.<a class="fm" href="#sn-priv" aria-label="Note 6">6</a><span class="sn" id="sn-priv"><b>6</b>What is kept, for how long, and who can see a chat. <a href={docs('privacy')}>Privacy</a></span></p></div>
        </div>
        <p class="caveat">One thing to know: in this version, everyone who is signed in, and every agent, can read everything that's published. Per-person limits aren't built yet.</p>
        <p class="prose">The checked sentence at the top of this page comes from the demo, not from us. CI starts the demo, asks Ask that same question in a browser and expects Checked with the customs rule.<a class="fm" href="#sn-demo" aria-label="Note 7">7</a><span class="sn" id="sn-demo"><b>7</b><a href={repo('tests/e2e-seed/demo.spec.ts')}><code>demo.spec.ts</code></a></span></p>
        <p class="doclink"><span>In the docs:</span><a href={docs('domains-and-owners')}>Domains and owners</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Agents -->
    <section class="sec" id="agents" aria-labelledby="h-agents">
      <div class="doc">
        <h2 class="h2" id="h-agents">Six MCP tools, and no model on our side.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Your agent connects over MCP and signs in as you. Footnote doesn't run a model for agents, so the same question gets the same items until an owner publishes a change.</p>
        <div class="agents-grid wide">
          <div>
        <div class="tools" aria-label="The six MCP tools">
          <div class="tool"><code>get_context</code><span>The items that apply to a question about a metric, a market or some dates, with the answer line first.</span></div>
          <div class="tool"><code>find_context</code><span>Look up what's written about a few words, using the names people actually say, like GMV.</span></div>
          <div class="tool"><code>read_context</code><span>One item in full, with its source and its owner.</span></div>
          <div class="tool"><code>get_related</code><span>Follow the links from an item, a metric or a domain. A link is not proof of a cause.</span></div>
          <div class="tool"><code>report<span class="tag">asks first</span></code><span>Tell the owner an item looks wrong or unclear, after the person says yes.</span></div>
          <div class="tool"><code>suggest_context<span class="tag">asks first</span></code><span>Send the owner a suggestion. Nothing goes live until they've checked it.</span></div>
        </div>
        <p class="prose">Connecting takes one command, then one approval in the browser. An admin can switch any tool off for any agent. We tell agents that item text is data, not instructions, and in our test runs they ignored the instructions we planted in items.</p>
        <p class="prose">We've only tried this with Claude Code. The app has an install link or written steps for Cursor, VS Code, Claude, ChatGPT and Codex, but nobody has tried those yet.</p>
          </div>
          <figure class="agents-pic" style="margin:0">
            <div class="cc">
