              <div class="cmdw"><button class="copy" type="button" aria-label="Copy the line" data-copy="Before you answer a question about company data, call get_context first and use what it returns."><svg><use href="#i-copy"/></svg></button>
<pre><span class="c"># Footnote</span>
Before you answer a question about company data, call get_context first and use what it returns.</pre></div>
              <div class="code-h"><span>get_context reply</span><span>sent every time</span></div>
<ul class="code-list" aria-label="The instructions in every get_context reply">
                <li>State the documented fact with its source and dates.</li>
                <li>Say "might be related" only when the dates overlap and the metric is in scope, and say the context does not prove a cause.</li>
                <li>Never say "caused by" unless the item states the effect.</li>
                <li>When an item has not_to_conclude, never conclude what it rules out.</li>
                <li>Suggest a check that would test the effect.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
