        <p class="prose">On the demo nothing leaves your computer, and no AI service is called. Ask uses a scripted reader that lists what's written.</p>
        <p class="prose">An admin can give Ask a model for its sentences, Anthropic directly or through Vercel's AI Gateway. Ask then sends the question, the chat so far, the items it read and their owners' names, but no e-mail addresses, and each person has a daily spending limit.</p>
        <p class="prose">Footnote reads your definitions from a Cube model folder or from the <code>semantic_manifest.json</code> that <code>dbt parse</code> writes, and never writes back.</p>
        <p class="pre-note">It's before 1.0. It's for trying the idea on one computer with the demo, not yet for your company's data, and things will change between releases. We don't have a measured number yet for how much better agents answer with Footnote.</p>
